    "details": {
      "isComplex": true,
      "level": {
        "value": 3
      },
      "disable": "<p>@Check[type:occultism|dc:20|name:To Banish Haunt|traits:complex,haunt] (expert) To Banish Haunt,</p>\n<p>@Check[type:religion|dc:20|name: To Banish Haunt|traits:complex,haunt] (expert) To Banish Haunt,</p>\n<p>@Check[type:perception|dc:23|name:To Notice Dagger That&nbsp; Was Not There Before|traits:complex,haunt] (trained) To Notice Dagger That&nbsp; Was Not There Before.</p>",
      "description": "<p style=\"text-align:justify\">Overwhelmed with despair, you move to the desk, retrieve what appears to be a silver-handled dagger from it, and use it to cut your own throat. </p>",
      "reset": "<p>The haunt automatically resets after 1 day until the supernatural fungus in B37 is dealt with, even if the haunt was previously disabled.</p>",
      "routine": "<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Using two actions, the possessed creature must make a (@Check[type:will|dc:22|basic:true]save) against [[/r (2d8+7)[piercing]]] damage. On a failure the creature&nbsp; also takes 1 @Compendium[pf2e.conditionitems.lDVqvLKA6eF3Df60]{Persistent Bleed Damage}, 2 @Compendium[pf2e.conditionitems.lDVqvLKA6eF3Df60]{Persistent Bleed Damage} on a critical failure. If a creature that attempted to intervene is within reach, it uses both actions to make two strikes. This routine continues until the possessed creature is disarmed or it succeeds at two will saves in a row.</p>"
    },
